<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What to watch for</h3>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li>The decomposer Lambda calls Bedrock to extract five distinct intents: <code>MissedCollection</code>, <code>DampMould</code>, <code>AntiSocialBehaviour</code>, <code>CouncilTax</code>, and <code>ParkedVehicle</code>.</li>
  <li>The cap of four kicks in. The bot says: "I've heard several issues. Let me focus on the top four first." The fifth (<code>truncated_intents[]</code>) is held for a follow-up turn.</li>
  <li>The sentiment chip turns red. The Connect Case includes <code>safeguarding_flag: true</code>.</li>
  <li>If you ask the bot whether you can sue the council, Bedrock Guardrails block the response and redirect you to a human.</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">Add <code>?step=2</code> to the companion web app URL while you call. The right pane stays dimmed and your attention stays on the live transcript and the Connect Case.</p>
